 "purpose": "The specifier-side fields (population, instances) for the 44 held-out negatives, so the expansion template can be applied to them symmetrically with the positives. A negative has no gold target and so no metadata to derive fields from; these are what an analyst asking for a construct the instrument does not hold would supply.",
 "method": "Written from each request's text alone, before any negative was scored under expansion and without looking up candidate instrument wording. Instances are one to three concrete examples or synonyms a domain analyst would list for the construct; population is set only where the request is about someone other than the participant (n44). Timeframe is left null on every row, mirroring the positives, where no metadata source exists for it.",
 "asymmetry_note": "Positives' instances come from the codebook's own option label; these come from an analyst's vocabulary. Arm P (population only) bounds what that asymmetry can contribute.",
